{"seq":54,"slug":"software-architecture-patterns","title":"软件架构模式","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns","rating":{"composite":3.68,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"软件架构模式\">软件架构模式</h1><p>架构是那些「改起来最贵」的决策的集合。一个函数写错了，下午就能改回来；可一旦选定了「整个系统拆成几十个微服务、各自一套数据库」，再想退回单体，往往要耗掉一个团队半年。正因为代价不对称，架构值得在动手写第一行业务代码之前被认真对待——但又不能过度提前，否则就成了为想象中的需求买单。这个 hub 想讲清楚的，正是这条钢丝怎么走。</p>\n<p>四个章节是一条层层递进的主线，而不是四堆并列的术语。</p>\n<p>第一条线是<strong>地基</strong>。在谈任何具体风格之前，得先说清「架构到底指什么」——它和详细设计的边界在哪、为什么有些决策不可逆；再说清架构服务于谁——可用性、可维护性、性能这些质量属性才是评判一个架构好坏的真正标尺；最后给出一张风格地图，让后面所有具体模式都能在图上找到自己的位置。</p>\n<p>第二条线是<strong>结构型</strong>：当所有代码还跑在同一个进程里时，怎么组织依赖与边界。分层架构、六边形与整洁架构、模块化单体，回答的都是同一个问题——如何让业务核心不被框架、数据库、UI 绑架。这是绝大多数系统真正待的地方，也是最容易被低估的一章。</p>\n<p>第三条线是<strong>分布式型</strong>：当一个进程装不下、一个团队管不过来时，系统跨进程、跨服务展开。从客户端-服务器与 SOA 的历史源头，到微服务的细粒度拆分，再到无服务器与事件驱动的极致解耦，这是一条「耦合越来越松、运维越来越重」的光谱。</p>\n<p>第四条线是<strong>决策与演进</strong>：架构不是一次性画完的图，而是一连串需要被选择、被守护、被记录的决策。怎么在众多风格里选型、怎么用适应度函数防止架构随时间腐化、怎么用 ADR 和 C4 把「为什么这么做」留给后来人。</p>\n<p>读法上，建议从地基顺着往下读：结构型是分布式型的内功，没有清晰的模块边界，拆成微服务只会把单体的烂摊子分散到网络上。而决策与演进这一章，则是回头审视前面所有选择的工具箱。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"architecture-vs-design","title":"架构与设计：决策的层次","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/foundations/architecture-vs-design"},{"seq":2,"slug":"quality-attributes","title":"质量属性与架构权衡","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/foundations/quality-attributes"},{"seq":3,"slug":"architecture-styles-overview","title":"架构风格总览","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/foundations/architecture-styles-overview"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"structural","title":"结构型","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/structural","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"layered-architecture","title":"分层架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/structural/layered-architecture"},{"seq":2,"slug":"hexagonal-clean","title":"六边形与整洁架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/structural/hexagonal-clean"},{"seq":3,"slug":"modular-monolith","title":"模块化单体","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/structural/modular-monolith"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"distributed","title":"分布式型","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/distributed","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"client-server-soa","title":"客户端-服务器与 SOA","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/distributed/client-server-soa"},{"seq":2,"slug":"microservices","title":"微服务架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/distributed/microservices"},{"seq":3,"slug":"serverless-eda","title":"无服务器与事件驱动架构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/distributed/serverless-eda"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"decisions","title":"决策与演进","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/decisions","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"choosing-architecture","title":"架构选型方法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/decisions/choosing-architecture"},{"seq":2,"slug":"evolutionary-architecture","title":"演进式架构与适应度函数","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/decisions/evolutionary-architecture"},{"seq":3,"slug":"documenting-architecture","title":"架构文档：ADR 与 C4","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-architecture-patterns/decisions/documenting-architecture"}]}]}